\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Exact decomposition of the copperplate-to-baseline cost gap for Memmingen (left) and as a distribution across the 135 synthetic networks (right). On Memmingen the topology main effect is measured with physics held identical to the copperplate; the physics-parameter difference between the copperplate and node-resolved configurations (return temperature, heating curve, heat-pump coefficient of performance) is shown separately so it is not attributed to spatial resolution. The additive identity closes to machine precision, so the terms are measured rather than fitted. The synthetic networks share physics across variants by construction and so carry no such term.}}{30}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:decomp}{{4}{30}{Exact decomposition of the copperplate-to-baseline cost gap for Memmingen (left) and as a distribution across the 135 synthetic networks (right). On Memmingen the topology main effect is measured with physics held identical to the copperplate; the physics-parameter difference between the copperplate and node-resolved configurations (return temperature, heating curve, heat-pump coefficient of performance) is shown separately so it is not attributed to spatial resolution. The additive identity closes to machine precision, so the terms are measured rather than fitted. The synthetic networks share physics across variants by construction and so carry no such term}{figure.4}{}}
